{"parentUuid":"f59878f9-e921-43dd-8c71-452b6bf1024f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdhDs4GpdQSnQSJfrTZt7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm comparing the UEFN interface layout against the current ZenRayMedia design to identify what's missing. Looking at the menu bar structure, UEFN has a traditional File/Edit/Asset/Window/Help menu with document tabs and parent class references, while the current version has a search bar with command palette, a brief selector, and icon buttons instead.\n\nThe palette section shows a stark difference too — UEFN uses a fine-grained category tree with typed icons, but the current design displays large cards in a horizontal grid layout. The viewport, details panel, hierarchy tree, animation timeline, and status bar are all either missing or significantly simplified in the current version. There's also a critical responsive design issue where everything collapses below 1100px width.\n\nThe real problem is that Chrome is only about 1000 CSS pixels wide, so the three-column layout never displays properly. I need to adjust the breakpoint down to 860px and reduce the minimum column widths. For the editor itself, I'll tighten the spacing from 14px to 6px gaps, reduce border radius from 20px to 8px, and redesign panel headers to include icons, titles, and close buttons. The main menu bar should contain actual dropdown menus (File/Edit/Component/Window/Help) with the actions currently scattered across icon buttons, mapping more closely to how UMG works.\n\nThe toolbar will have dedicated icons for Save, Open, and Compile actions. For the palette, I'm replacing the large component cards with a compact tree view showing categories like Common (Image, Text) and Containers (Canvas, Grid, Overlay, etc.), but since containers aren't implemented yet in V1, I should either disable them with a \"V2\" tag or hide them entirely to avoid showing non-functional entries.\n\nThe hierarchy panel will display the document structure as a real tree with Canvas and its child pieces, each with lock and visibility toggles. The content editor that was in the blocks section should move into the Details panel as a tab, similar to how UEFN organizes its interface.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the tab structure for the Details panel — it needs Détails for properties, Contenu for the brief and blocks, plus Sorties, Thèmes, Critique, Forge, and Journal to keep everything accessible. But there's a challenge: the four-directional drop editing that currently works on the structure zone relies on detecting cursor position within item rectangles. If I convert the hierarchy to a thin tree, that drag-and-drop behavior gets harder to execute on left/right edges, though top/bottom placement should still work geometrically.\n\nRather than risk losing that functionality, I'll keep the four-side drop indicator on the tree rows themselves — they'll be about 24 pixels tall, which gives enough horizontal space across the ~230-pixel width to distinguish left, right, and center zones. Before I finalize this approach, I should check how the drag handler actually computes placement to see if it's percentage-based or pixel-based.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7688,"cache_read_input_tokens":135488,"output_tokens":2011,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7688,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2011,"cache_read_input_tokens":135488,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7688,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7688},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdhDs1CnA6hcy4B6g3zx1","type":"assistant","uuid":"c2eeebad-b2bb-44